{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1415252-what-company-made-white-wolf-s-dice","id":1415252,"title":"What company made White Wolf's dice?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-23T17:49:26-07:00","id":1415252,"title":"What company made White Wolf's dice?","content":"I assume the company that actually physically made the various WW dice are unedited.<br /> <br /> If I am correct, does anyone know who the actual manufacturers were?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T18:19:43-07:00","id":1415254,"title":"","content":"White Wolf had multiple dice sets. A quick search on the database for the person with the largest dice collection in the world, Kevin Cook, showed a Changeling and Vampire set made by Q-Workshop. Those dice are towards the end and fit other dice I've bought from Q-Workshop. You can probably find more dice information on dice collecting forums.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.dicecollector.com/MINT63.HTM\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://dicecollector.com/images/small/ed/94581f72332bb4ba32d2210ad75596.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.dicecollector.com/MINT63.HTM\" target=\"_blank\"> DiceCollector.com's DICE - MISCELLANEOUS #63 </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.dicecollector.com/MINT63.HTM\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.dicecollector.com/MINT63.HTM </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> dice, dice collecting, dice collector, dice collection, d4, d6, d8, d10, d12, d20 </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T18:35:24-07:00","id":1415257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1415252-what-company-made-white-wolf-s-dice#post1415252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume the company that actually physically made the various WW dice are unedited.<br /> <br /> If I am correct, does anyone know who the actual manufacturers were?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The original sets? No idea. The <a href=\"https://thumbs.worthpoint.com/zoom/images4/1/0417/10/mage-ascension-dice-set_1_f6058e45edb131b07f3731050d9fdeac.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">packaging</a> only had White Wolf's contact information in them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T01:53:49-07:00","id":1415279,"title":"","content":"I've been trying to research this myself . It depends on the set, and whether they were official or not; it's sometimes hard to tell with Masquerade dice in particular. There were a LOT of <b>Vampire </b>and &quot;vampire&quot; dice on the market back in the day.<br /> <br /> I think some of them were made custom by Chessex, and few more generic ones were <i>probably </i>from Koplow (at least for some of the NWoD sets), but there's another company(?) that made the bulk of the ones that came in the little velvet bags: the dice are bulkier and rounder than Chessex dice, and often have a speckled finish. I'm pretty sure they were generic dice that were customized, because the Time of Judgment dice and the Vampire: The Requiem dice are almost exactly the same, except for the numbers.<br /> <br /> I've not been able to figure out what that brand was. I was quite literally trying to Google this information not two hours ago. If anyone has a clue on this, I'd also love to know.<br /> <br /> (for reference, this is the style I'm talking about<b></b>: <a href=\"https://i.redd.it/hzu8uyx4s1x21.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://i.redd.it/hzu8uyx4s1x21.jpg</a>)<br /> <br /> Edit: I suspect it <i>was </i>Chessex or Koplow, but they might just not make them anymore, or they really were made just for White Wolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 09-24-2020, 05:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}